# Overleaf upload bundle: regenerate from overleaf/ (see overleaf/README.md)
research/nongaussian-bp/overleaf-bp-diffusion.zip
# Any zip of overleaf/ made for uploading to Overleaf's web editor -- a local
# convenience, not a build artifact worth tracking, and it drifts stale the
# moment the source changes underneath it.
/overleaf.zip
*.zip

# --- kept locally for reference, not for a reviewer's eyes ---
# Internal revision/process notes -- not thesis content.
# The university's own copyrighted guide PDFs -- no reason to redistribute.

# Deploy stamp written by hpc/stamp_revision.sh. Regenerated per deploy, so a
# committed copy would always be stale and would itself dirty the tree it records.
research/nongaussian-bp/REVISION

# LaTeX build products. Each document is compiled in its own folder now.
overleaf/*/main.pdf
# ...except the four rendered PDFs themselves: tracked deliberately so the
# thesis, paper, workshop and compendium are readable straight from GitHub
# without a local build. Keep these current by rerunning overleaf/build.sh
# and committing the result after any content change -- a stale committed PDF
# would be worse than none, since a reader has no way to tell it's stale.
!overleaf/paper/main.pdf
!overleaf/workshop/main.pdf
!overleaf/thesis/main.pdf
!overleaf/compendium/main.pdf
overleaf/*/*.aux
overleaf/*/*.bbl
overleaf/*/*.blg
overleaf/*/*.log
overleaf/*/*.out
overleaf/*/*.toc
overleaf/*/*.lof
overleaf/*/*.lot
overleaf/*/*.fls
overleaf/*/*.fdb_latexmk
overleaf/*/*.synctex.gz

# Editorial notes and the Bocconi guides are now TRACKED. They used to be
# ignored, and an `rm -rf` of the old thesis/ tree on 18 Aug 2026 destroyed the
# working copies precisely because git could not see them.

# Superseded historical research, kept on disk but not tracked. It is ~150 MB of
# old notebooks and drafts whose successors are all in research/ -- worth having
# locally, not worth carrying in every clone. See archive/README.md.
archive/

# External advisor review, kept local: not our writing and not for distribution.
research/Review-GPT.md
